WEBVTT

NOTE
The words that appear on screen in the walkthrough. The film has no speech.
Times come from video/launch/demo/timeline.js. A chip by the phone says Sample entries
for the whole walkthrough.

00:00.250 --> 00:02.800
Daksha, a quick look
Recorded from the app, with made-up sample entries. Typing is sped up.

00:03.700 --> 00:06.200
Step 1 of 7: Say hello
Daksha shows you around the first time you open it.

00:06.300 --> 00:15.200
Step 2 of 7: Write a day
A few lines about what happened. It is saved when you press Save entry.

00:15.300 --> 00:20.600
Step 3 of 7: Open any entry
See what Daksha learned from it, and the entries like it.

00:20.700 --> 00:26.000
Step 4 of 7: See what Daksha knows
Every memory shows the entry it came from. Fix it or forget it.

00:26.100 --> 00:31.800
Step 5 of 7: Record a voice note
The screen shows when the microphone is on.

00:31.900 --> 00:40.400
Step 6 of 7: Daksha asks before it acts
Anything that leaves Daksha waits for your yes.

00:40.500 --> 00:53.500
Step 7 of 7: Make it yours
Make a face, make someone to talk to, and pick your reminders.

00:54.950 --> 00:58.400
Daksha. A friendly assistant that remembers your life.
